</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7cb8caa-c0bf-11f1-ac40-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/MONTAGE-SHOSHAN-HARAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7cb8caa-c0bf-11f1-ac40-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/MONTAGE-SHOSHAN-HARAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1f7defb8-be59-11f1-b751-855272092b6e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 15:01:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel warns Gazans will pay 'heavy price' for any October 7 attacks on military</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261006-israel-warns-gazans-will-pay-heavy-price-for-any-october-7-attacks-on-military</link><description>
Israel on Tuesday said that Hamas and the Palestinian population in Gaza would pay a "heavy price" if any of Israel's armed forces were harmed on the three-year anniversary of the militant group's October 7 attack. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe623a8-c158-11f1-ab65-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278512155571.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe623a8-c158-11f1-ab65-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278512155571.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6ce7df2-c158-11f1-aa3b-77497fb40820</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 07:50:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe623a8-c158-11f1-ab65-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278512155571.jpg">© Oded Balilty, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi-backed Yemeni forces expel the Houthis from several areas around key strait, officials say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-backed-yemeni-forces-expel-the-houthis-from-several-areas-around-key-strait-officials-say</link><description>
Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces staged a lightning advance on ​Monday to retake the coast around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait up to the city of Mocha, the government said, pushing the Iran-backed Houthis out of most of the areas they seized last month. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06e24072-c0f1-11f1-8ede-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4580563926ac3f725bc3d82-10617721.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06e24072-c0f1-11f1-8ede-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4580563926ac3f725bc3d82-10617721.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">974c9294-c0f0-11f1-9f81-71ed274b3f93</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 19:17:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>ISIS suspects face 'outsourced' justice in Iraq as HRW warns of 'collective global detention crisis'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-crisis-1</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Letta Tayler, Senior Counterterrorism Advisor at Human Rights Watch. She warns of the detention of suspected Islamic State members transferred from northeast Syria to Iraq as part of a much wider "global detention crisis". The men and boys now held in Iraq are living in 'dire' conditions, including deaths from illness, allegations of torture, and serious questions surrounding access to effective legal representation. Can accountability be achieved through legal proceedings that respect the rule of law and provide genuine justice to both detainees and victims?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f0c0f28-c0cb-11f1-abfc-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-151326-152657-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f0c0f28-c0cb-11f1-abfc-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-151326-152657-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2424c5e0-c0cb-11f1-834e-a9d28765d43a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 15:46:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis claim attacks on Riyadh airport as Saudi-led forces strike Yemen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261005-yemen-military-announces-broad-range-of-strikes-against-houthis-in-bid-to-retake-lost-territory</link><description>
Iran-backed Houthis said Monday they had struck Riyadh's international airport and an Aramco refinery as Saudi-led forces intensified attacks on Houthi positions in Yemen in a bid to retake territory. Pakistan and Turkey also pledged troops to Saudi Arabia under a new defence pact. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3df66fda-c091-11f1-a1a7-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265728988880.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3df66fda-c091-11f1-a1a7-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265728988880.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">70aafcd4-c091-11f1-9280-d31aef42a17f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 08:12:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3df66fda-c091-11f1-a1a7-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265728988880.jpg">© Ansar Allah Media Office via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran says no military solution to war as peace talks with US stall</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-iran-us-military-middle-east-war-peace-talks</link><description>
