The ​leader of ​Yemen's Saudi-backed government announced the beginning of a ​major ‌military ⁠operation against the Iran-backed Houthis ‌on Sunday aimed at ⁠recapturing territory under their control. The announcement came as Houthi forces cut off a vital supply route to the besieged government-held city of Taiz, according to several security sources.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c14ee92e-c08d-11f1-b754-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T135414Z-2043951740-RC2DWNA2JWYI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c14ee92e-c08d-11f1-b754-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T135414Z-2043951740-RC2DWNA2JWYI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8f53ebc8-bff1-11f1-91cc-b955e607a27f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 12:59:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c14ee92e-c08d-11f1-b754-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T135414Z-2043951740-RC2DWNA2JWYI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-1.jpg">© via REUTERS - Yemen News Agency</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>West Bank: Palestinians ‘harassed’ by settlers’ increasing use of drones</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones</link><description>
Palestinians and activists report an increased use of drones in the occupied West Bank, particularly by the army and settlers, to whom the government supplies the drones directly. The drones are used to intimidate, monitor, demolish and make daily life unbearable.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad046c8-bd7a-11f1-b57d-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Pic-Drones.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad046c8-bd7a-11f1-b57d-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Pic-Drones.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72da03b6-be74-11f1-bf6c-41e1b8a52073</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 12:01:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad046c8-bd7a-11f1-b57d-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Pic-Drones.png">© The Observers / Herd of Justice</source><dc:creator>Marguerite Ipek LACROIX</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel prepares to mark October 7</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-prepares-to-mark-october-7</link><description>
An Israeli strike on a civilian vehicle in Gaza on Sunday killed one Palestinian and wounded at least 11 others. Israel’s military said it was targeting a Hamas militant. Palestinians have reported a surge in Israeli fire and airstrikes across Gaza over the past month, with more than 75,000 people killed and much of the enclave destroyed. Meanwhile, Israelis held their weekly protest in Tel Aviv’s Hostages Square, the last before Wednesday marks three years since the October 7 attack. Protesters said they wanted to commemorate the victims and demand an independent state inquiry into the events and decisions that led to the attack. The Hamas-led assault killed around 1,200 people in Israel and saw more than 250 others taken hostage, according to Israeli authorities. Rachael Goldberg Polin, an American-Israeli activist and mother of slain hostage Hersh Goldberg-Polin, speaks to France 24.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9482b6e4-bfe0-11f1-9696-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-120715-121646-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9482b6e4-bfe0-11f1-9696-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-120715-121646-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">99316d34-bfe0-11f1-8d20-8fa7ddd26abe</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 10:59:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Who are the mystery pilots who successfully landed endangered Flydubai flight 1073?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-who-are-the-mystery-pilots-who-successfully-landed-endangered-flydubai-flight-1073</link><description>
A passenger on Flydubai flight 1073 has described the actions of on-duty crew members who rushed into the cockpit to stabilise and land the plane after the co-pilot attacked the captain with a crash axe. The flight carrying 182 people en route to Israel Wednesday was able to make an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia after a descent so extreme that part of its rudder was torn away. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da1105dc-bfcf-11f1-8542-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273485606536-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da1105dc-bfcf-11f1-8542-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273485606536-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8218d5c8-bfcd-11f1-a3ed-df9ae4e03873</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 09:36:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da1105dc-bfcf-11f1-8542-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273485606536-1.jpg">© Ariel Schalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen’s Houthis claim attacks on Aramco facilities in Riyadh</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-attacks-on-aramco-facilities-in-riyadh</link><description>
Yemen’s Houthi rebels have claimed responsibility for attacks in Riyadh, including on facilities belonging to Aramco, the world’s largest oil company. This follows reports from residents of flames and smoke rising from an oil facility on the outskirts of the Saudi capital. Meanwhile, the Houthis have accused Saudi Arabia of launching dozens of strikes on Sanaa, warning that they will continue to respond to any escalation with further escalation. Here’s Jennie Shin with more on the situation on the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f23d5188-bfca-11f1-bb16-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-090624-090759-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f23d5188-bfca-11f1-bb16-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-090624-090759-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f759acd4-bfca-11f1-b895-5fa848c9c018</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 08:21:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
